tory\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div>",
  "textContent": "The Beatles attended a meditation session with Maharishi Mahesh Yogi in London, on the evening of 31 August 1967. The band first met Maharishi on 24 August, and the following day travelled to Bangor in north Wales to attend a conference on Transcendental Meditation. That trip was curtailed after news broke of the death of their manager Brian Epstein. They returned to London that day.A meditation session was held on 31 August, although the precise location is not known. The only photographer present, Philip Townsend, recalled it being at an address on Abbotsbury Road, W14, but the book The Beatles’ London says the likeliest address was 4 Albert Place, W8.Attending the session were The Beatles, Jane Asher, Maureen Starkey, Mike McCartney, and various others. The primary purpose was to receive solace and continue the group’s meditation progress.\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 1 September 2025Also on this day...2019: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Vina Robles Amphitheatre, Paso Robles2003: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Marymoor Amphitheatre, Redmond2001: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Concord Pavilion, Concord1973: Mixing: Meat City by John Lennon1969: Lennon, Harrison and Starr watch Bob Dylan perform at the Isle of Wight Festival1967: The Beatles issue a statement on NEMS Enterprises1965: The Beatles live: Cow Palace, San Francisco1964: Day off in Cape May, New Jersey1963: The Beatles live: Odeon Cinema, Southport1962: The Beatles live: Town Hall, Lydney1961: The Beatles live: St John’s Hall, Liverpool1960: The Beatles live: Indra Club, HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
